    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Shared Dreamwork.</strong> You extend your dreamspace outward, creating a temporary link between your consciousness and another's.</p><p><strong>Once per Soma Break</strong>, as an action, choose one willing creature within 6 squares. For 10 minutes, you and the linked creature share a dream-channel:</p><ul><li><strong>Dream-Link Insight (Soul):</strong> Both gain +1 Insight (Soul), and you may use either creature's Insight (Soul) bonus on Insight (Soul) checks.</li><li><strong>Emotional Mirror:</strong> Once during the link, when the ally fails a Soul or Presence check, you may use your reaction to let them reroll the save, adding your Soul value.</li><li><strong>Shared Omen:</strong> Once during the link, you or the ally may add +1d4 to an attribute check, attack roll, or defense check after seeing the roll but before knowing the result.</li></ul><p>During Shared Dreamwork, Sparks and metaphysical disturbances become easier for the ally to perceive, and certain Bad Eden travel, intrigue, and encounter systems may offer additional insights.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
